Usage:
  x2c script [options] <file> [<argument>...]

Run an x2c source file as a script. The first run builds an executable in
the per-user cache; later runs start it directly until the script, a file
it includes or imports, the compiler, the runtime, or an option changes.

Target options:
  -j, --jobs <count>          Maximum parallel translation and compilation jobs

Output options:
      --source-map            Map generated C locations to original x2c sources
      --rebuild               Build the script even when its cached executable is current
      --clean                 Remove the script's cached build and exit without running it

Translation options:
  -I <dir>                    Add a shared x2c/C include directory
      --x-include-dir <dir>   Add an x2c-only include directory
      --c-include-dir <dir>   Add a C-only ordinary include directory
      --c-system-dir <dir>    Add a C-only system include directory
      --package-dir <dir>     Add a directory of x2c packages

C compiler options:
      --cc <program>          Use <program> as the host C compiler
  -O0, -O1, -O2, -O3, -Os     Set C optimization
  -g                          Emit debug information
  -D <name>[=<value>]         Define a C preprocessor macro
  -U <name>                   Undefine a C preprocessor macro
  -Xcc <arg>                  Pass one argument only to C compilation
  -pthread                    Enable native threading for compilation and linking

Linker options:
  -L <dir>                    Add a library search directory
  -l <name>                   Link library <name>
      --rpath <dir>           Search <dir> for shared libraries when the program runs
  -Wl,<arg>[,<arg>...]        Pass comma-separated arguments to the linker
  -framework <name>           Link a native framework on macOS
  -Xlinker <arg>              Pass one argument to the linker

General options:
  -h, --help                  Show help and exit
  -v, --verbose               Show commands as they are executed
  -###                        Show commands without executing them
      --plain                 Use stable output without terminal rendering
      --color <auto|always|never>
                              Control terminal color
      --debug                 Enable compiler debug logging
      --max-errors <count>    Stop after <count> errors per unit (default: 20)
      --diagnostics-file <file>
                              Write compiler diagnostics to <file> as JSON Lines
  @<file>                     Read additional options from a response file

Every word after <file> is passed unchanged to the script, including
words that begin with - or @. A script whose first line is the shebang
'#!/usr/bin/env -S x2c script' runs directly. The cache is X2C_CACHE_DIR,
XDG_CACHE_HOME/x2c, or ~/.cache/x2c. Builds remove the entries of
scripts that no longer exist.
